{%- doc -%}
  A divider: a horizontal rule, optionally with a short line of text centred in it.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- comment -%}
  A labelled divider -- a short line of text centred between two horizontal rules, e.g.
  "o envíanos un mensaje" between a WhatsApp CTA and a form. Mirrors
  ../design-system/src/components/Divider/Divider.tsx and spends its tokens. Built as its own block (not inlined into whatever composition
  needed it first) because it is reused across at least two page compositions --
  templates/page.contacto.json originally had this exact markup/CSS hand-rolled inside
  blocks/mionas-contact-form.liquid, which owned no business rendering decorative copy between two
  sibling blocks it doesn't control. See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-12-contacto-page-design.md.

  Text renders through snippets/mionas-text.liquid so Text Size reuses the same
  ../design-system/src/components/Text/Text.tsx role vocabulary every other Mionas text block does,
  rather than this block inventing its own type scale. Colour is NOT one of the exposed settings,
  though: this always spends --divider-text-foreground (secondary ink), not Text's own
  colour axis -- ".text-role.mionas-divider__text" beats ".text-role--<color>" on specificity for
  the same reason blocks/mionas-price.liquid's ".text-role.mionas-price" does (see that file). A
  divider is secondary copy by definition. The rule's own colour is a setting (Subtle or Strong), since the
  page heading on /collections needed a strong rule under its title.

  WIDTH IS FIXED AT 100%, NOT A SETTING. A divider that does not span its container has nothing to
  divide -- shrink-to-fit is never the wanted behaviour, unlike blocks/mionas-text.liquid or
  blocks/mionas-stamp.liquid, which are properly inline-ish elements. This was the original bug
  reported after this block's first version shipped: the outer <div> shrank to its own text width
  inside its parent group's column layout (every Mionas block earns this by an explicit width
  setting; this one hard-codes it because there is no legitimate use case for a narrower divider).

  ::before/::after keep the two lines out of the DOM so the text can be centred with plain flex gap
  rather than manual width math -- moved verbatim from the original .mionas-contact-form__divider.

  THE LINE RENDERS EVEN WITH BLANK TEXT. Only the text and the second line are gated on
  `block_settings.text` (one line, so the gap doesn't split it) -- a divider with no label is
  still a divider, not nothing. This differs
  from most Mionas blocks (e.g. mionas-text itself), where blank content means the whole block
  renders nothing; a divider's job is the rule, and the text is a label on top of it, not the
  reason it exists.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings

  # Each size is a text role, as in Divider.tsx.
  assign text_variant = 'body'
  if block_settings.size == 'sm'
    assign text_variant = 'label'
  endif
%}
<div
  class="mionas-divider mionas-divider--{{ block_settings.thickness | default: 'thin' }} mionas-divider--{{ block_settings.color | default: 'subtle' }} spacing-style"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings %}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <span class="mionas-divider__line"></span>
  {%- if block_settings.text != blank -%}
    {%- render 'mionas-text',
      content: block_settings.text,
      variant: text_variant,
      tag: 'span',
      class: 'mionas-divider__text'
    -%}
    <span class="mionas-divider__line"></span>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .mionas-divider {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--divider-base-gap);
    width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .mionas-divider__line {
    flex: 1;
    height: var(--divider-thin-border-width);
    background: var(--divider-subtle-border-color);
  }

  .mionas-divider--thick .mionas-divider__line {
    height: var(--divider-thick-border-width);
  }

  /* Strong is body ink: a section rule under a heading rather than a quiet hairline between form
     parts. */
  .mionas-divider--strong .mionas-divider__line {
    background: var(--divider-strong-border-color);
  }

  /* (0,2,0), same trick blocks/mionas-price.liquid's ".text-role.mionas-price" uses -- beats the
     ".text-role--<color>" class snippets/mionas-text.liquid also applies, at (0,1,0), so this
     block's own muted colour always wins regardless of bundle order. See the file header comment
     for why colour is fixed rather than a setting. */
  .text-role.mionas-divider__text {
    color: var(--divider-text-foreground);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Divider",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "o",
      "info": "Leave empty for a plain line."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "size",
      "label": "Text Size",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "sm",
          "label": "Small"
        },
        {
          "value": "md",
          "label": "Medium"
        }
      ],
      "default": "md",
      "info": "Small uses Label text, Medium Body.",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.text != blank }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "thickness",
      "label": "Thickness",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "thin",
          "label": "Thin"
        },
        {
          "value": "thick",
          "label": "Thick"
        }
      ],
      "default": "thin"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color",
      "label": "Color",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "subtle",
          "label": "Subtle"
        },
        {
          "value": "strong",
          "label": "Strong"
        }
      ],
      "default": "subtle",
      "info": "Subtle is the light hairline used between form parts; Strong is body ink, for a rule under a heading."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Divider",
      "category": "t:categories.basic"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
